    "summary": "A man&#039;s cap made of seal skin; shape akin to a coif.  Framing the face a red tabby wool cloth with nap, bordered by a narrow strip of cream seal skin (in stitched sections).  Main part of cap made of segments of pale coloured fur stitched together; mostly worn away.  Oval piece at back of head, made of sealskin (?) (without fur).  Tied under chin with flat interlaced braid with cream, blue and green glass (?) beads at bifurcated ends.  Tassels made from recycled red and black tabby woollen cloth.  Damaged; fragile.",
